  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1409.03 Restrictions on Burning",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1409.03 Restrictions on Burning.\n\n(a) Off-specification used oil shall be burned only in the following devices:\n\n(1) Industrial furnaces;\n\n(2) Boilers, as defined in Env-Hw 103, that are:\n\na. Industrial boilers located on the site of a facility engaged in a manufacturing process where substances are transformed into new products, including the component parts of products, by mechanical or chemical processes; or\n\nb. Utility boilers used to produce electric power, steam, heated or cooled air, or other gases or fluids for sale;\n\n(3) Used oil-fired space heaters under the provisions of Env-Hw 1406.04; or\n\n(4) Hazardous waste incinerators subject to regulation under Env-Hw 300 and Env-Hw 700.\n\n(b) Specification used oil shall be burned only in the following devices:\n\n(1) Oil furnaces and boilers that are not located at private residences, hotels, motels, apartment buildings, and residential institutions including hospitals, residential treatment facilities, and nursing homes;\n\n(2) Used oil-fired space heaters, provided the heater is designed to have a maximum capacity 0.5 million Btu per hour, and combustion gases from the heater are vented to the outside ambient air; or\n\n(3) Any device specified in (a), above.\n\n(c) Used oil containing greater than or equal to 2 ppm PCBs shall be burned in compliance with 40 CFR 761, pursuant to the Toxic Substances Control Act.\n\n(d) Prior to burning used oil, the owner or operator of a device in (b)(1) or (b)(2), above, shall determine whether the used oil meets the specifications in Env-Hw 1404.02 by:\n\n(1) Performing analyses of the used oil as specified in Env-Hw 1404.01;\n\n(2) Applying knowledge that the used oil has not been mixed or contaminated with any other wastes, provided that the used oil is either:\n\na. Automotive used oil generated by the used oil burner; or\n\nb. Household DIY used oil received directly from household DIY used oil generators; or\n\n(3) If the used oil was received from a used oil processor/re-refiner or used oil fuel marketer subject to Env-Hw 1408 or Env-Hw 1410, respectively, using information provided for each shipment of used oil.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
}
